{
  "score_support": "supports_wrong_score",
  "score_support_basis": "理由把引用定义当成明确锚点，并把“doesn't really make sense”当成充分具体问题，主要推出 CoT 的 5 分；但真实标签为 3，即定位不够可信、只说明问题性质。",
  "error_sentences": [
    {
      "sentence": "This allows the authors to accurately identify the referenced definition.",
      "error_type": "rubric_misapplication",
      "explanation": "该句断言作者能准确锁定位置，从而满足 5 分的明确 grounded 门槛；但评论真正质疑的是与未指明的“former sentence”的关系，按真实标签 3 作者并不能自信确定所指部分，不能据此升到 5。"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "The comment then specifies the issue: the definition is inadequate because a large difference in privacy risks can occur when users’ data are dissimilar, and it questions the logical connection to the previous sentence, stating that it \"doesn't really make sense.\"",
      "error_type": "evidence_misread",
      "explanation": "把箭头左侧疑似论文原文“definition is inadequate because...”误当作评审者自己对问题的具体说明；评审者实际只说与前一句的关系不清楚、不合理，证据归因错误并高估了 specificity/grounding。"
    }
  ],
  "overall_basis": "CoT 理由的证据链整体服务于错误的 5 分，而非真实的 3 分；核心错误是误读引用边界并误用 grounded 门槛。"
}
